

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 9

                                  FOR

                   SHAMAN UGA-BUGA MAKUMBU





  Quote of the Week:

  Imperial Motto of Frederick III (1415-1493), Holy Roman Emperor and ruler 
of Austria:
  "The whole world is subject to Austria"


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  With the advent of the spring season, Uga-Buga Makumb set out to quench 
his thirst for adventure.  He cast a Skeletal Army spell and the 154th 
Skeletal Legion, the 233rd Skeletal Chariots and the 71st Skeletal Legion 
arose from the graves of the dead!
  Quantara Roo was magically flooded.  Magical tornadoes hit the defenders 
of Ngara.  The Tornado affected no armies in Ngara.
  With the coming of the early summer season Uga-Buga Makumb boldly marched 
his forces into St Helens (#402).

  A great host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Mountain province of St Helens, 
held by Hokuto (#4).  St Helens was overrun by Uga-Buga Makumb's host.  St 
Helens was found to have an income of 4 gold.

  II Kahn (#6)'s forces initiated a campaign of conquest directed at Bir 
Nzaran, a Desert province owing allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Kahn commanded the invading armies.  
The defenders were led by the provincial garrison commander.  The armies 
were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Bir Nzaran (1203):

            188th   
            Bowmen  
