 Garrison  Garrison 
                    
  DEFENDING ARMY

  II Kahn led a host of loyal soldiers.  No generals were present to lead 
the forces of Uga-Buga Makumb.
  Kahn's soldiers, with no camels for the tortuous desert campaign, suffered 
from thirst.  The acting commander's soldiers, ill-supplied in the tortuous 
desert, suffered from thirst.  The battle was a fair fight, as no luck of 
any great importance appeared to affect the overall course of the engagement 
before it commenced.  In this perilous chess match, Kahn seemed to gain the 
tactical edge.

  Out on the right wing, the Veteran 220th Light Cavalry faced the 133rd 
Garrison.  On this field, the craven fear of a single soldier worked against 
the 133rd Garrison.  They were thrown into disarray when he ran, shouting 
"We're all cooked!"  The 220th Light Cavalry fought the 133rd Garrison and 
advanced at will.
  Out on the left outside flank, the Veteran 218th Legion were blessed by a 
band of priests sent by the League of Pagan Clerics, which inspired them to 
a fanatical zeal.  They were arrayed against the 166th Garrison.  The 188th 
Bowmen flanked the enemy and attacked with full force.  The 218th Legion 
fought the 166th Garrison and smashed their heads as if they were eggplants.
  Kahn's armies shattered the army opposing them with a final charge.  The 
220th Light Cavalry demolished the 133rd Garrison.  The 218th Legion 
scattered the 166th Garrison in all directions.
  Bir Nzaran was overrun by Kahn's forces in a bloody campaign.  The acting 
commander withdrew to the Callisto Sea.
  Midsummer's night passed and a pleasant late summer came.  Uga-Buga Makumb 
moved into Belladonna (#302) with his army.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll sent an invasion force into the 
adjacent Forest province of Belladonna, owned by Prometeo (#5).  
Uga-Buga Makumb commanded the invading armies.  The defending forces were 
commanded by Girard (#15).  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as 
shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Belladonna (0302):

                     233rd/S            
                     Chariots           
