  DEFENDING ARMY

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll stood ready at the head of his 
thousands.  Girard marched with his loyal troops, jaws set in terrible 
determination.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll strode forward and 
challenged Girard to personal combat.  Girard refused to enter personal 
combat.
  The forces commanded by Girard were disappointed by his faint-heartedness. 
They marched on, though with lessened confidence.  Luckily, Uga-Buga Makumb 
managed to convince a savage native tribe to surprise Girard with their 
fleet footed skirmishers.  With this help, Uga-Buga Makumb gained an 
important advantage.  Also, his wise tactical planning assured his forces an 
undeniable advantage.

  On the left outside flank, the Veteran 71st Skeletal Legion were arrayed 
against the 160th Legion.  The 315th Dragons soared over the 160th Legion 
and attacked them.  The 71st Skeletal Legion battled with the 160th Legion 
and smashed their skulls as if they were eggplants.
  In the interior front, the Veteran 316th Bowmen faced the 168th 
Heavy Cavalry.  The 316th Bowmen battled the 168th Heavy Cavalry and mowed 
them down like weeds.
  Within the interior lines, the Veteran 317th Trolls were overflown by the 
Circle of Wraiths, who urged them into mindless fanatical battle-lust with 
their maniacal laughter.  They faced the 199th Heavy Cavalry.  The 293rd 
Dragons soared over the 199th Heavy Cavalry and attacked them.  The 317th 
Trolls fought the 199th Heavy Cavalry and smashed them like rotten tomatoes.
  On the right wing, the 154th Skeletal Legion were arrayed against the 
152nd Legion.  The 314th Dragons swooped down on the 152nd Legion and 
attacked them.  The 154th Skeletal Legion battled with the 152nd Legion and 
smashed their heads as if they were eggshells.
  Uga-Buga Makumb's great horde overwhelmed the army of Prometeo (#5) and 
took the field, dispersing their enemies.  The 71st Skeletal Legion 
scattered the 160th Legion in all directions.  The 316th Bowmen slew the 
168th Heavy Cavalry almost to a man.  The 317th Trolls demolished the 199th 
Heavy Cavalry.  The 154th Skeletal Legion annihilated the 152nd Legion.
  Belladonna was overrun by the forces of Uga-Buga Makumb.  The battle 
affected the quality of our forces:  the 316th Bowmen proved its mettle in 
the fight and we now rate it a Crack unit.  His forces completely dispersed, 
Girard (#15) escaped alone to Marzuq.

  II Kahn (#6)'s forces initiated a campaign of conquest in Ravenwood, a 
Forest province owing its allegiance to Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  
Kahn's forces conquered Ravenwood without any major engagements.  Kahn leads 
approximately 1 Bowmen, 1 Legion and 1 Light Cavalry.
  With the coming of the fall season Uga-Buga Makumb failed in his attempt 
to cast a Plague spell.
  Amberleaf was magically flooded.  A diplomatic furor erupted between the 
Realms of Agesilao (#9) (whose alliances are too incompatible) and 
Uga-Buga Makumb, degrading their diplomatic relations 1 level(s)!
  Sherwood was hit by a plague.  The plague struck the 87th Garrison and the 
88th Garrison in Sherwood and destroyed them.
  The fall cooled into a frigid early winter.  Uga-Buga Makumb attempted an 
illegal move.  He was ordered to move from Belladonna to Plumwood, further 
than his army could move.  So, he worked hard on his Tactics but was 
thwarted in his efforts.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll for this 
year.


  Uga-Buga Makumb treated with his ally Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  The captain of the 30th Eagles felt a thirst for adventure awakening in 
his breast, and speaking eloquently of the lands and princes of Katanga, 
persuaded his men to march with him to Katanga.

  Cantia was plundered by the Werewolf, who stormed from out of the dark and 
pillaged or destroyed 2 gold worth of property.  Ngara was raided by 
the Succubus, who came from out of the dark wilderness and pillaged or 
destroyed 3 gold worth of property.  Starhaven was plundered by the Gargoyle,
who stormed from out of the dark wilderness and pillaged or destroyed 3 gold 
worth of property.  The Icaria Sea was plundered by the Giant Wolverine, who 
stormed from out of the dark wilderness and pillaged or destroyed 2 gold 
worth of property.  Sherwood was plundered by the Centaur, who came from out 
of the dark wilderness and pillaged or destroyed 2 gold worth of property.  
Quantara Roo was plundered by the Imp, who came from out of the dark 
wilderness and pillaged or destroyed 1 gold worth of property.
  Here is the financial report for Uga-Buga Makumb's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 308 gold in revenue.  63 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 0th Garrison, the 1st Garrison, the 9th Garrison, the 18th 
Garrison, the 22nd Garrison, the 85th Garrison, the 130th Garrison, the 
145th Garrison, the 146th Garrison, the 147th Whales, the 148th Garrison, 
the 173rd Garrison, the 176th Garrison, the 181st Garrison, the 264th 
Garrison, the 272nd Garrison and the 273rd Legion trained well and improved 
in quality.  158 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Uga-Buga Makumb 
was left with 189 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Guerin
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I cast a Kill Enemy spell and Charious was magically killed by 
a dark Necromantic spell!  And so it came to pass that Charious met his 
tragic end.
  Windy spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  I cast a Bless 
spell.  The Dolphin Sea was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless 
affected no armies in the Dolphin Sea.
  In late summer, I cast a Bless spell.  The Jellyfish Sea was magically 
blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in the Jellyfish Sea.
  During fall, I attempted an illegal move.  I tried to move from Quantara 
Roo to Rejaf, but provincial flooding and insufficient transport thwarted 
the move.  So, I really tried hard to improve my Tactics, but I practiced in 
vain.  I conducted military exercises and the 124th Skeletal Dragons 
improved in quality.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  I tried to move from Quantara 
Roo to Kajaani, a non-adjacent province.  This is illegal!  Instead, I tried 
to improve my Tactics, but the task seemed beyond my natural aptitude.

  Thy humble servant,   Guerin


From: Gunga Din, Squire to Teleko
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to sweet spring.  Ningarl was resurrected by the spell 
cast by Teleko.  His efforts improved his aptitude in White Magic.
  With the coming of the early summer season Teleko's attempted cast of the 
Skeletal Army spell was unsuccessful.
  In late summer, Teleko flew over to Amberleaf.  To the north, the 
landscape is marred by a broad expanse of ice.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Amberleaf, a 
Forest area owned by Hokuto (#4).  Teleko's armies took possession of 
Amberleaf practically uncontested.  Amberleaf was discovered to have a tax 
base of 5 gold.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into fall.  Teleko rode his flying 
armies into Birchwood.  To the west there is a Jungle province known as the 
El Kalaa Sea (#201), a land of Humans where Prometeo rules.  Their Human 
fighters prefer to fight as Legion.  To the north icy wastes stretch to join 
the far horizon.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Birchwood, a 
Forest area owned by Prometeo (#5).  Teleko's armies took possession of 
Birchwood practically uncontested.  Birchwood was found to have a tax base 
of 10 gold.
  In early winter, Teleko rode his flying armies into the El Kalaa Sea.  
Southwest of here lies the province of Mare Imbrium (#102), ruled by 
Prometeo.  It is known to be a Sea province inhabited by no races.  To the 
west lies a Forest area called Alderwood (#101), populated by Dragons.  It 
is ruled by Prometeo.  If need be, they can muster an army of Dragons to 
defend their territory.  To the north is a forbidding land of ice which 
seemingly has no end.  Teleko also discovered a Crypt (#75) in the El Kalaa 
Sea, occupied by the Chimera.  Legend says the Huge Hoard of Gold is hidden 
here.  The Chimera is a powerful but unintelligent winged monster with the 
body of a lion and three heads, of lion, dragon and goat.

  An army sent by the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded 
the El Kalaa Sea, hoping to subjugate that province ruled by Prometeo and 
made up of great Jungles.  The El Kalaa Sea was overrun and occupied by 
Teleko's host.  The El Kalaa Sea was found to have an income of 3 gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Teleko


