From: Odysseus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I rode my flying armies over to Gnarlia.  To the north, the 
landscape is scarred by an unending expanse of frigid ice.

  A great host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Forest province of Gnarlia, held 
by II Kahn (#6).  Odysseus's forces took Gnarlia without any major 
engagements.  Gnarlia was found to have an income of 3 gold.
  With the coming of the early summer season, I rode my flying armies over 
to Peachwood.

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Uga-Buga Makumbian empire 
marched on the Forest province of Peachwood, a land garrisoned by the 
soldiers of II Kahn.  Odysseus's forces experienced little resistance in 
Peachwood and I there established our reign.  Peachwood was discovered to 
have a tax base of 6 gold.
  Midsummer's night passed and a pleasant late summer came.  I rode my 
flying armies into Bronzeleaf.

  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
invaded Bronzeleaf, hoping to subjugate that province owned by II Kahn and 
made up of great Forests.  I was in command of the attacking armies.  The 
defending forces were led by Hawkins (#56).  The armies were drawn up into 
lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Bronzeleaf (1303):

  123rd     102nd             
  Eagles    Eagles            
