  63rd/G    52nd/A    68th/A  
  Legion    Bowmen    Bowmen  
                              
  DEFENDING ARMY

  I led a host of loyal soldiers.  Hawkins led his armies into the battle.
  I was not very lucky this time, because a strong wind blew into my men's 
faces, giving Hawkins's men a small edge.  Further, my careful tactical 
plans did not succeed against Hawkins's clever counterstrokes, and my men 
entered battle with a slight tactical disadvantage.

  On the left wing, the Crack 334th Bowmen were arrayed against the Green 
63rd Legion.  The 206th Dragons soared over the 63rd Legion and attacked 
them.  The 334th Bowmen fought the 63rd Legion and smashed their skulls as 
if they were eggplants.
  In the interior front, the Veteran 198th Trolls faced the 52nd Bowmen.  
The 91st Dragons soared over the 52nd Bowmen and attacked without mercy.  
The 91st Dragons were decimated by the bolts loosed by the dangerous Bowmen. 
The 102nd Eagles were bothered by the fire of their feared Bowmen nemesis.  
In this match, the 198th Trolls obtained the upper hand when they ordered 
their trumpeters to disrupt the signals of their enemy.
  The ongoing struggle went on with a murderous fury.  A captain of the 52nd 
Bowmen perceived an opening in the enemy lines which had opened when they 
skirted a large rock outcropping.  By charging into the gap, the 52nd Bowmen 
gained a considerable advantage.  In spite of the 52nd Bowmen's good 
fortune, the 198th Trolls fought the 52nd Bowmen and overpowered them with 
their thundering charge.
  Out on the right wing, the Veteran 333rd Bowmen were arrayed against the 
68th Bowmen.  The 249th Dragons soared over the 68th Bowmen and attacked 
without mercy.  The 249th Dragons were decimated by the bolts fired by the 
pesky Bowmen.  In this match, the 333rd Bowmen's commander released a herd 
of pink-painted elephants to make his opponents believe they were going 
insane, but the ruse had little effect except to amuse them.  The 333rd 
Bowmen fought the 68th Bowmen and advanced at will.
  Odysseus's great horde overpowered the army of Kahn (#6) and took the 
field, scattering their enemies.  The 334th Bowmen scattered the 63rd Legion 
in all directions.  The 198th Trolls destroyed the 52nd Bowmen.  The 333rd 
Bowmen annihilated the 68th Bowmen.
  Odysseus's host ended the campaign successfully and conquered Bronzeleaf.  
The battle affected the quality of our forces:  the 206th Dragons proved its 
valor during the fight and we now rank it a Veteran unit.  We can raise the 
rating of the 249th Dragons to Veteran, its men having displayed especially 
admirable elan.  The mayhem wreaked by the 123rd Eagles in the battle has 
raised the spirits of its warriors, and all agree that it has achieved 
Veteran quality.  We could not have been better satisfied with the fighting 
spirit of the 102nd Eagles, and we have elevated its rating to Veteran.  His 
forces completely dispersed, Hawkins (#56) fled frightened and alone to Bir 
Nzaran.
  With the advent of the fall season I rehearsed and practiced my Sageness 
and improved noticeably.  I invented nothing in my sagely researches.
  During early winter, I tried to practice my Sageness, but the task was 
beyond my aptitude.  I discovered nothing in my sagely experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Odysseus


