  With the coming of the early winter season I could not recruit more 
Garrison in Cherrywood because the provincial maximum had already been 
recruited.  So, I practiced my Tactics well but could not improve my Tactics.

  Thy humble servant,   Clarambald


From: Constantine
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I boldly marched my forces into the Daedalus Sea (#702).
  The wet spring blossomed into early summer.  I recruited enough men in the 
Daedalus Sea to form the 85th Garrison for the army of the provincial 
garrison commander.
  I heard of a feature in Starhaven (#701): a Maze occupied by the Troll, 
who holds the Large Hoard of Gold.
  With the coming of the late summer season I boldly marched my forces into 
Kilkenny (#801).  Viewing the eastern horizon, a man can see a Sea province 
known as Mare Actium (#901).  It is said that no one is the ruler there.  It 
is known to be populated by no races.  To the north icy wastes extend to 
join the far horizon.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Kilkenny, a Plain 
area owned by Hokuto (#4).  Kilkenny was overrun and occupied by Constantine
's host.  Kilkenny was discovered to have an income of 5 gold.
  With the advent of the fall season I announced a plea for recruits in 
Kilkenny and was able to form the 9th Garrison to fight for the provincial 
garrison commander.
  In early winter, I attempted an illegal move.  I was ordered to move from 
Kilkenny to Starhaven, further than my army could move.  Instead, I tried 
hard to improve my Tactics, but I practiced in vain.

  Thy humble servant,   Constantine


From: Pascal
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I marched on Cantia (#403) with my formidable forces.  I made 
some side trips while marching through Cantia and now 100% of Cantia has 
been explored.  I was informed by some sheepherders of a feature in Cantia, 
a Dungeon (#82) inhabited by the Werewolf.  What treasure may lie there is 
unknown.  Those who stalk the night fear the Werewolf, a man with the 
ability to turn into a wolfman or even a full wolf.  According to legend, he 
who is severely bitten by the werewolf is cursed to become one himself.

  A host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Plain province of Cantia, ruled 
by Prometeo (#5).  Pascal's forces encountered little opposition in Cantia 
and I there established our reign.  Cantia was discovered to have a tax base 
of 6 gold.
  In early summer, I attempted a Skeletal Army spell, but bungled it.
  Midsummer's night came and went and a pleasant late summer came.  I 
recruited enough men in Cantia to form the 176th Garrison and the 264th 
Garrison for the army of the provincial garrison commander.
  With the advent of the fall season I moved into Marzuq (#303) with my 
high-spirited army.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll's minions initiated a campaign of 
conquest directed at Marzuq, a Desert province owing its allegiance to 
Prometeo.  Pascal's forces took Marzuq without any major engagements.  
Marzuq was found to have an income of 1 gold.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  I announced a plea for 
volunteers in Marzuq and was able to enlist the 130th Garrison to fight for 
the provincial garrison commander.

  Thy humble servant,   Pascal


From: Gunga Din, Squire to Alaric
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, Alaric set out to quench his thirst 
for adventure.  He cast a Skeletal Army spell and the 184th Skeletal Bowmen 
arose from the graves of the dead!
  The wet spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  Alaric disbanded 
the 214th Fleet.  The 214th Fleet dug graves for themselves, unwilling to 
serve anyone but their master, unless given to an Undead leader like 
themselves.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Alaric marched his command into 
Damnonia (#1402).  Viewing the northeastern horizon, a man can see a Forest 
province known as Elkhome (#1501).  It is said that no one is the ruler 
there.  It is known to be populated by Ents.  They can muster an army of 
Ents to defend their province.  East of here lies the province of Maplehaven 
(#1502), ruled by Giovanna d'Arco.  It is known to be a Forest province 
inhabited by Elves.  Their Elven fighters traditionally fight as Bowmen and 
Heavy Cavalry.  The terrain of Maplehaven appeared to be Plain, but Alaric's 
Ultraviolet Lenses revealed the actual terrain.  Alaric was told by some 
sheepherders of a perilous feature in Damnonia previously unknown to us, a 
Tomb (#80) inhabited by the Ice Devil.  What treasure may lie there is 
unknown.  Legend has it that the Ice Devil is an extraordinarily cruel, cold 
and very powerful devil with magical powers.  Alaric also discovered a Cave 
(#110) in Damnonia, occupied by the Black Dragon.  What treasure may lie 
there is unknown.  The Black Dragon is an Evil and very powerful 
acid-spitting dragon.

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Uga-Buga Makumbian empire 
marched on the Plain province of Damnonia, a land garrisoned by the forces 
of II Kahn (#6).  Alaric's forces encountered little resistance in Damnonia 
and Alaric there established our reign.  Damnonia was discovered to have an 
income of 2 gold.
  With the advent of the fall season Alaric cast a Plague spell.  Quantara 
Roo was hit by a plague.  The plague struck the 109th Heavy Cavalry, the 
240th Bowmen, the 241st Bowmen and the 292nd Legion in Quantara Roo and 
destroyed them.  Alaric's experience raised his prowess in Necromancy.
  Your characters of this high level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- "GATE DEMON" SPELL (abbreviated "GD"):  By the dark power of 
this spell, an extra-dimensional gate is opened to the nether worlds, from 
where a demon is summoned to fight in place of the spellcaster.  The caster 
has no control over what type of demon will appear.  If the Demon wins, it 
will return to the Abyss from whence it came.  If it loses, the caster must 
continue the fight at the current combat range.  If another Mirror Image or 
Gate Demon spell is cast against it, both spells will be nullified.  A Demon 
may refuse to fight an opponent of Evil to Undead alignment (50% chance).  
Note: with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 28".

  During early winter, Alaric marched his forces into Maplehaven (#1502).  
Maplehaven had an illusion cast upon it.  It was actually a Forest province. 
Looking to the northeast, one can see a Sea area, which is known as the 
Andrea Doria Sea (#1601).  It is populated by no races and no one rules 
there.  To the east lies a Forest area called Sageleaf (#1602), populated by 
Humans.  It is ruled by Giovanna d'Arco.  Their Human fighters fight in the 
style of Legion.  Southeast of here lies the poor province of Kajaani 
(#1603), ruled by Giovanna d'Arco.  It is known to be a Plain province 
inhabited by Werefolk.  If need be, they can call on a host of Were-Beasts 
to defend their province.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll sent an invasion force into the 
adjacent Forest province of Maplehaven, owned by Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  
Alaric's forces conquered Maplehaven without any major engagements.  
Maplehaven was discovered to have an income of 6 gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Alaric


From: Marlboro
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I explored Gafsa thoroughly, leaving no stone unturned, and our 
exploration level there has risen to 100%.
  Windy spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  I levied the 148th 
Garrison in Gafsa to serve the provincial garrison commander.
  In late summer, I journeyed to the Daedalus Sea.  I made some side trips 
while marching through the Daedalus Sea and now 100% of the Daedalus Sea has 
been explored.
  With the coming of the fall season I tried to explore the Daedalus Sea but 
it seemed that it had already been completely explored.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  I travelled to Berga.

  Thy humble servant,   Marlboro


From: Kari
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I rode into Belladonna.  West of here lies the province of 
Plumwood (#202), ruled by Prometeo.  It is said to be a Jungle province 
inhabited by Humans.  Their Human fighters fight in the style of Legion and 
Elephants.  To the northwest lies a rich Forest province named Birchwood 
(#301), populated by Humans.  It is ruled by Prometeo.  Their Human warriors 
prefer to array themselves as Legion and Heavy Cavalry.
  With the advent of the early summer season, I cast a Skeletal Army spell 
and no skeletons answered the spell's call.
  Midsummer's day passed and a pleasant late summer arrived.  I moved into 
Marzuq.  Turning to the southwest, one espies a rich Plain area, which is 
known as Orielle (#204).  It is populated by Humans and Bradipo I rules 
there.  Their Human warriors prefer to array themselves in the style of 
Legion and Chariots.  West of here is Tesawa (#203), a poor Mountain 
province ruled by Prometeo, where Humans dwell.  Their Human warriors fight 
in the style of Legion.
  During fall, I journeyed to Orielle.  To the southeast there is a Jungle 
province known as Mongu (#305), a rich land of Humans where 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango rules.  Their Human fighters fight in the 
style of Legion and Light Cavalry.  Viewing the southwestern horizon, a man 
can see a Jungle province known as Macondo (#205).  It is said that 
Bradipo I is the ruler there.  It is known to be populated by Orcs.  Their 
Orcish fighters fight in the style of Phalanx.  West of here lies the 
province of Waterford (#104), ruled by Prometeo.  It is known to be a Sea 
province occupied by no races.
  With the coming of the early winter season, I travelled to Waterford.  To 
the southwest lies a Desert area called Bam Yanga (#105), populated by 
Humans.  It is ruled by Giovanna d'Arco.  Their Human warriors array 
themselves as Camel Corps.  Looking to the west, one espies a Jungle area, 
which is known as Maicuru (#1804).  It is populated by Humans and 
Giovanna d'Arco rules there.  Their Human warriors array themselves as 
Legion.  Northwest of here is Darkwood (#103), a Sea province ruled by 
Prometeo, where no races dwell.

  Thy humble servant,   Kari


From: Everard
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter melted into sweet spring, and I prepared to carry out my 
imperial assignments.  I was instructed in White Magic by Elmer.  I 
practiced well and improved my ability in White Magic.
  During early summer, I was instructed in White Magic by Elmer.  I 
practiced for many weeks and my skill in White Magic increased.
  Speaking to some friendly farmers, I heard a rumor about a Cavern in Bir 
Nzaran (#1203), occupied by the Ice Devil.  They maintain that the Ice Devil 
actually owns the Huge Hoard of Gold.
  With the advent of the late summer season I was tutored in the art of 
Necromancy by Garin.  I practiced my Necromancy and my skill in Necromancy 
went up.
  The summer mellowed into fall.  I was instructed in Necromancy by Garin.  
I practiced my Necromancy and improved substantially.
  During early winter, I was tutored in the art of Necromancy by Garin.  I 
tried to practice my Necromancy, but the task was beyond my ability.

  Thy humble servant,   Everard


From: Gunga Din, Squire to Garin
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, Garin set out to quench his thirst 
for adventure.  He searched the Sacred Rock with every intention of 
overcoming it and whatever guardian beast lay within.  Garin encountered 
the Giant Eagle.  Uttering his syllables of magic with breathless precision, 
Garin let fly a Fireball spell and scored 11 damage points on 
the Giant Eagle.
  The Giant Eagle moved into bow range.  Garin waved his arms and gestured 
mightily, meaning to cast an Ice Suspension spell, but it backfired and a 
rabbit tumbled out of his hat instead.
  The Giant Eagle rushed lustily into melee combat.  The Giant Eagle 
summoned all its will and bravely slashed at its vaunted enemy but its aim 
was just off the mark.  Garin's spell was disrupted by the event.  Garin 
shifted over to a better attacking vantage.  Then Garin swang at 
the Giant Eagle and scored on the Giant Eagle, inflicting 7 points of 
damage.  The Giant Eagle fell, mortally injured.  Garin took the treasure 
chest that once belonged to the Giant Eagle.  Garin secured the Large Hoard 
of Gold.  Garin found 14 gold in the treasure of the Giant Eagle.
  While scouting the Sacred Rock, Garin saw a Statue which seemed to be of a 
magical nature.
  Magic runes formed on the Statue, saying "The Statue will gamble with you 
for any amount of gold you have in your Kingdom's treasury.  When you scout 
it, SA-y how much you wish to gamble, and whoever rolls the highest number 
with two dice takes the gold.  In case of a tie, the Statue wins!"  During 
his travels this season, Garin was ambushed, pinned down and bloodied up by 
wild-eyed soldiers.  Garin finally escaped.  A Royal Marshal tracked Garin 
down.  But he was obviously no renegade spy, and that got Garin off the 
hook.

  With the advent of the early summer season Garin could not cast a Bless 
spell because Garin had no skill in White Magic.  So, Garin tried to 
practice his Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his ability.  He 
discovered nothing in his sagely experiments.
  With the advent of the late summer season Garin practiced his Necromancy 
well but could not improve his skill in Necromancy.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  Garin practiced 
his Necromancy for many weeks, but could make no significant headway.
  In early winter, Garin tried to practice his Necromancy, but the task was 
beyond his natural ability.

  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Garin


From: Gladstone
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I recruited enough men in Quantara Roo to form the 0th Garrison 
and the 1st Garrison for the army of Gladstone.
  Windy spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  Charious was 
resurrected by the spell cast by me.
  In late summer, I could not cast Resurrection on Charious because Charious 
was still alive.  Instead, I really tried hard to improve my Necromancy, but 
I practiced in vain.
  With the advent of the fall season Gladstone's Earthquake spell fizzled 
and I was left covered with psycho-kinetic goo.
  The fall season cooled into the stillness of early winter.  I attempted an 
illegal move.  I tried to move from Quantara Roo to Damnonia, but provincial 
flooding and insufficient transport thwarted the move.  So, I worked hard on 
my Archery but was thwarted in my self-improvement efforts.

  Thy humble servant,   Gladstone


From: Ningarl
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  During early summer, I spoke urgently to Dreux of the greatness of the 
King's empire and convinced Dreux to pledge his services to the King.  After 
talking to Dreux, I judged him (a Human well known for Tactics) to have an 
Evil, Berserk nature.
  With the coming of the late summer season I announced a plea for recruits 
in Cherrywood and was able to form the 272nd Garrison to fight for the 
provincial garrison commander.
  The summer surrendered to the fall.  I rode into Silvermist.
  In early winter, I led no armies, so I didn't execute my order to Leave 
All.  So, I discovered nothing in my sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Ningarl


From: Dreux
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In late summer, I moved into Amberleaf.
  With the advent of the fall season, I enlisted the 22nd Garrison in 
Amberleaf to serve the provincial garrison commander.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  I journeyed to Birchwood.

  Thy humble servant,   Dreux


From: Charious
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I was magically killed by a dark Necromantic spell!  And so it 
came to pass that I met my tragic end.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer arrived.  I recruited enough 
men in Quantara Roo to create the 273rd Legion and the 292nd Legion for the 
army of the provincial garrison commander.
  With the coming of the fall season, I moved into Bronzeleaf.  I discovered 
an interesting feature in Bronzeleaf: a Magic Pool (#124) inhabited by 
the Mermaid.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  The Mermaid is a 
female creature with the tail of a large fish and a magical charming 
ability.
  In early winter, I levied the 173rd Garrison and the 181st Garrison from 
among the population of Bronzeleaf, to serve under the provincial garrison 
commander.

  Thy humble servant,   Charious


