GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT

Kingdom of Babba Sissoko (#0):
  In late summer, Saladin (#14) sailed into Mare Tarkium.  Saladin located a 
previously unknown Catacombs in Mare Tarkium, inhabited by the Black Dragon.
  In fall, Saladin wandered far and wide in Mare Tarkium, exploring its 
mysteries.  Saladin was informed by some peasants of a perilous feature in 
Mare Tarkium previously unknown to us, an Ancient Megaliths where dwells 
the Werewolf.
  In early winter, Saladin explored Mare Tarkium carefully, leaving no stone 
unturned.
  In spring, Tlazolteotl (#88) flew into Shasta.
  Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0)'s minions initiated a campaign of 
conquest directed at Shasta, a Mountain province owing allegiance to 
Prometeo (#5).  Tlazolteotl (#88) was in command of the attacking armies.  
The defending forces were commanded by the provincial Eagle chieftain.  
Shasta was overrun by the forces of Tlazolteotl.

Kingdom of Mugai (#3):
  In early winter, Mugai (#3) treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Mugai 
(#3) treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Mugai (#3) treated with his ally 
II Kahn (#6).  Mugai (#3) treated with his ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Mugai 
(#3) treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Mugai (#3) treated with his ally 
Agesilao (#9).
  In early summer, Samantha (#95) rode into Tabora.
  In late summer, Samantha travelled to Ngara.

Kingdom of Hokuto (#4):
  In spring, Hokuto (#4) journeyed to Cherrywood.
  In late summer, Hokuto travelled to Amberleaf.


Kingdom of Prometeo (#5):
  In spring, Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0)'s minions initiated a 
campaign of conquest directed at Shasta, a Mountain province owing 
allegiance to Prometeo (#5).  Tlazolteotl (#88) was in command of the 
attacking armies.  The defending forces were commanded by the provincial 
Eagle chieftain.  Shasta was overrun by the forces of Tlazolteotl.
  In early summer, Girard (#15) marched his forces into Belladonna (#302).
  In late summer, Girard marched with his loyal troops, jaws set in terrible 
determination.

  On the right outside flank, the Veteran 71st Skeletal Legion were arrayed 
against the 160th Legion.  The 315th Dragons soared over the 160th Legion 
and attacked them.  The 71st Skeletal Legion battled with the 160th Legion 
and smashed their skulls as if they were eggplants.
  In the interior front, the Veteran 316th Bowmen faced the 168th 
Heavy Cavalry.  The 316th Bowmen battled the 168th Heavy Cavalry and mowed 
them down like weeds.
  Within the interior lines, the Veteran 317th Trolls were overflown by the 
Circle of Wraiths, who urged them into mindless fanatical battle-lust with 
their maniacal laughter.  They faced the 199th Heavy Cavalry.  The 293rd 
Dragons soared over the 199th Heavy Cavalry and attacked them.  The 317th 
Trolls fought the 199th Heavy Cavalry and smashed them like rotten tomatoes.
  On the left wing, the 154th Skeletal Legion were arrayed against the 152nd 
Legion.  The 314th Dragons swooped down on the 152nd Legion and attacked 
them.  The 154th Skeletal Legion battled with the 152nd Legion and smashed 
their heads as if they were eggshells.  His forces completely dispersed, 
Girard escaped alone to Marzuq.

Kingdom of Kahn (#6):
  In early summer, Kahn (#6) boldly marched his forces into Bir Nzaran 
(#1203).
  In spring, Hawkins (#56) recruited enough men in Bronzeleaf to form the 
63rd Legion for the army of Hawkins.
  In late summer, Hawkins led his armies into the battle.

  On the right wing, the Crack 334th Bowmen were arrayed against the Green 
63rd Legion.  The 206th Dragons soared over the 63rd Legion and attacked 
them.  The 334th Bowmen fought the 63rd Legion and smashed their skulls as 
if they were eggplants.
  In the interior front, the Veteran 198th Trolls faced the 52nd Bowmen.  
The 91st Dragons soared over the 52nd Bowmen and attacked without mercy.  
The 91st Dragons were decimated by the bolts loosed by the dangerous Bowmen. 
The 102nd Eagles were bothered by the fire of their feared Bowmen nemesis.  
In this match, the 198th Trolls obtained the upper hand when they ordered 
their trumpeters to disrupt the signals of their enemy.
  The ongoing struggle went on with a murderous fury.  A captain of the 52nd 
Bowmen perceived an opening in the enemy lines which had opened when they 
skirted a large rock outcropping.  By charging into the gap, the 52nd Bowmen 
gained a considerable advantage.  In spite of the 52nd Bowmen's good 
fortune, the 198th Trolls fought the 52nd Bowmen and overpowered them with 
their thundering charge.
  Out on the left wing, the Veteran 333rd Bowmen were arrayed against the 
68th Bowmen.  The 249th Dragons soared over the 68th Bowmen and attacked 
without mercy.  The 249th Dragons were decimated by the bolts fired by the 
pesky Bowmen.  In this match, the 333rd Bowmen's commander released a herd 
of pink-painted elephants to make his opponents believe they were going 
insane, but the ruse had little effect except to amuse them.  The 333rd 
Bowmen fought the 68th Bowmen and advanced at will.  His forces completely 
dispersed, Hawkins fled frightened and alone to Bir Nzaran.
  In early winter, Hawkins travelled to Sherwood.


